133
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:04,704
[WHIRRING]

134
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:04,704
[HORSES WHINNYING]

135
00:05:04,704 --> 00:05:06,806
HUH. LET'S GO.

136
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:09,876
[WESTERN DRAWL]
LET'S ROUND US UP SOME COWS.
COME ON, ISABELLA!

137
00:05:09,876 --> 00:05:11,377
YEE-HAW!

138
00:05:11,377 --> 00:05:15,081
OOH...

139
00:05:15,081 --> 00:05:16,516
[WHINNIES]

140
00:05:16,516 --> 00:05:20,720
[MOOING]

141
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,088
[CELL PHONE RINGS]

142
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,088
OH, MY GOSH!

143
00:05:22,088 --> 00:05:24,190
STACY? I'M, LIKE,
IN A STAMPEDE.

144
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:25,525
IT'S LIKE--

145
00:05:25,525 --> 00:05:28,428
[MOOING]

146
00:05:25,525 --> 00:05:28,428
UH, JUST A SEC.

147
00:05:28,428 --> 00:05:29,996
HEY, CANDACE.

148
00:05:28,428 --> 00:05:29,996
HEY, PHINEAS.

149
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:31,898
PHINEAS?

150
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:31,898
[HORSES WHINNYING]

151
00:05:31,898 --> 00:05:33,666
Candace: PHINEAS!

152
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:38,037
STACY, I GOT TO GO.

153
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:38,037
[SQUEALS]

154
00:05:38,037 --> 00:05:47,680
[MOOING]

155
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,015
[ALL YELLING]

156
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:51,451
[MOOING]

157
00:05:51,451 --> 00:05:54,020
[HORSES WHINNYING]

158
00:05:54,020 --> 00:06:00,793
[WOMEN SCREAMING]

159
00:06:00,793 --> 00:06:06,432
YEE-HAW! HYAH, COW!

160
00:06:06,432 --> 00:06:07,433
[GUITAR PLAYING]

161
00:06:07,433 --> 00:06:09,102
♪ IN THE MALL ♪

162
00:06:09,102 --> 00:06:11,137
♪ UP AND DOWN
THE ESCALATORS ♪

163
00:06:11,137 --> 00:06:12,205
♪ IN THE MALL ♪

164
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:14,574
♪ I GOT A HANKERIN'
FOR POTATERS ♪

165
00:06:14,574 --> 00:06:16,309
♪ IN THE MALL ♪

166
00:06:16,309 --> 00:06:17,977
♪ 'CAUSE PRETTY SOON
NOW IT'LL ♪

167
00:06:17,977 --> 00:06:19,812
♪ BE ABOUT TIME
TO STOP FOR VITTLES ♪

168
00:06:19,812 --> 00:06:21,814
♪ IN THE MALL ♪

169
00:06:21,814 --> 00:06:25,385
[ALL CHEWING]

170
00:06:25,385 --> 00:06:27,487
WELL, THAT WAS
DELICIOUS.

171
00:06:27,487 --> 00:06:30,123
[MOOING]

172
00:06:30,123 --> 00:06:33,726
Phineas: HYAH!

173
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:36,562
A STAMPEDE THROUGH DOWNTOWN.
I MEAN, WHO DOES THIS?

174
00:06:36,562 --> 00:06:38,398
THOSE TWO ARE
SO GOING TO GET IT.

175
00:06:38,398 --> 00:06:40,066
AAH! AAH!

176
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:47,807
UNH!

177
00:06:47,807 --> 00:06:49,142
[BELL RINGS]

178
00:06:49,142 --> 00:06:51,811
[WESTERN DRAWL]
WELL, WHAT CAN I
DO YOU FER, LITTLE LADY?

179
00:06:51,811 --> 00:06:53,312
WHAT HAVE YOU GOT
TO STOP A STAMPEDE?

180
00:06:53,312 --> 00:06:55,148
I THINK I MIGHT HAVE
JUST THE THING FOR YOU.

181
00:06:55,148 --> 00:06:59,318
LET ME JUST CHECK...
A SCARY WOLF PUPPET!

182
00:06:59,318 --> 00:07:01,354
IMAGINE YOU'RE A COW.

183
00:07:01,354 --> 00:07:03,022
YOU'RE THERE MINDING
YOUR OWN BUSINESS,

184
00:07:03,022 --> 00:07:04,690
CHEWING YOUR CUD
WITH THE OTHER HEIFERS

185
00:07:04,690 --> 00:07:06,259
WHEN SUDDENLY--[HOWLS]

186
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:08,761
"I'M A VERY HUNGRY WOLF.
I LIKE TO EAT COWS.

187
00:07:08,761 --> 00:07:12,565
"OOH, I'M SO HUNGRY."

188
00:07:12,565 --> 00:07:15,201
[RATTLING]

189
00:07:15,201 --> 00:07:17,103
UH, NO, OF COURSE NOT.

190
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:19,539
OH, A GENUINE
SILENT COW WHISTLE.

191
00:07:19,539 --> 00:07:20,973
YOU'RE SURE THIS
WILL STOP A STAMPEDE?

192
00:07:20,973 --> 00:07:22,975
AS SURE AS
THE DAY IS LONG.

193
00:07:22,975 --> 00:07:23,976
SOLD!

194
00:07:23,976 --> 00:07:25,645
[BELL RINGS]

195
00:07:25,645 --> 00:07:26,813
[MOOING]

196
00:07:26,813 --> 00:07:30,583
[NO AUDIO]

197
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:32,285
WELL, WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

198
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:35,221
IT WORKS!

199
00:07:35,221 --> 00:07:37,723
WAIT! STOP! UH-OH.

200
00:07:37,723 --> 00:07:38,958
AAH!

201
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:40,426
[NO AUDIO]

202
00:07:40,426 --> 00:07:47,767
HEY, THIS COW WHISTLE
DOESN'T WORK.

203
00:07:47,767 --> 00:07:50,303
OOH, THEY'RE SO
GOING TO GET IT.

204
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:53,306
MOM, THEY'RE DRIVING
A HERD OF CATTLE
RIGHT THROUGH DOWNTOWN.

205
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:54,941
WELL, UM,
I'M A LITTLE BUSY, SWEETIE.

206
00:07:54,941 --> 00:07:56,709
I'M HAVING
MY HAIR DONE AT BABS.

207
00:07:56,709 --> 00:07:59,479
OH, YEAH, THAT'S PERFECT!
OH, THEY'RE COMING YOUR WAY.

208
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:02,048
QUICK, LOOK OUT THE WINDOW!
DO YOU SEE ANY COWS?

209
00:08:02,048 --> 00:08:05,952
Mom: THAT'S CUTE, CANDACE.

210
00:08:05,952 --> 00:08:07,720
OK, BABS NEEDS
TO COMB ME UP.

211
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:10,556
GOT TO GO.

212
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:10,556
[GRUMBLES]

213
00:08:10,556 --> 00:08:13,726
ANY LAST NOISES,
PERRY THE PLATYPUS?

214
00:08:13,726 --> 00:08:15,795
YOU KNOW, THAT LITTLE
CHIRPING SILLY NOISE
THAT YOU MAKE?

215
00:08:15,795 --> 00:08:17,263
[CHATTERING]

216
00:08:15,795 --> 00:08:17,263
THAT'S THE ONE!

217
00:08:17,263 --> 00:08:23,536
[LAUGHS]

218
00:08:23,536 --> 00:08:24,770
WAIT, DON'T TOUCH
THAT BUTTON!

219
00:08:24,770 --> 00:08:26,639
NO, NO, THE OTHER ONE.
YES, THAT ONE!

220
00:08:26,639 --> 00:08:28,774
THAT'S THE ONE
YOU SHOULD NOT TOUCH!

221
00:08:28,774 --> 00:08:29,842
[ALARM BUZZING]

222
00:08:28,774 --> 00:08:29,842
[DOOFENSHMIRTZ GASPS]

223
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:31,878
Computer: SELF-DESTRUCT
SEQUENCE INITIATED.

224
00:08:31,878 --> 00:08:33,713
NOW YOU'VE GONE
AND DONE IT!

225
00:08:33,713 --> 00:08:36,682
YOU PUT A SELF-DESTRUCT
 BUTTON IN A DEATH CHAMBER?

226
00:08:36,682 --> 00:08:38,084
I'M SO OUT OF HERE.

227
00:08:38,084 --> 00:08:40,553
THIS IS THE WORST
"BRING YOUR DAUGHTER
TO WORK" DAY EVER.

228
00:08:40,553 --> 00:08:42,221
TELL YOUR MOTHER
YOU HAD FUN, THOUGH.

229
00:08:42,221 --> 00:08:43,155
OH, BY THE WAY,

230
00:08:43,155 --> 00:08:44,924
I'M TAKING
THE LAST ESCAPE POD.

231
00:08:44,924 --> 00:08:48,394
Doofenshmirtz: IT'S OK.
I'LL JUST TAKE THE JET PACK.

232
00:08:48,394 --> 00:08:50,129
NOW, WHERE DID I PUT THAT--

233
00:08:50,129 --> 00:08:51,631
OH, WHAT WAS I THINKING?

234
00:08:51,631 --> 00:08:53,232
I PUT THE JET PACK
IN THERE, TOO?

235
00:08:53,232 --> 00:08:55,134
I MIGHT AS WELL
HAVE GIVEN HIM
AN ESCAPE HATCH.

236
00:08:55,134 --> 00:08:58,237
I MEAN...

237
00:08:58,237 --> 00:09:00,406
WELL...GUESS I'M RUNNING.

238
00:09:00,406 --> 00:09:03,476
[SCREAMING]

239
00:09:03,476 --> 00:09:06,879
Doofenshmirtz: HELP ME!

240
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:09,782
HELP! UNH! AAH!

241
00:09:09,782 --> 00:09:13,986
WAIT, GO BACK! I FORGOT
MY LITTLE WOODEN HEAD!

242
00:09:13,986 --> 00:09:15,021
YES!

243
00:09:15,021 --> 00:09:17,557
YES, WE ARE SAFE!

244
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:20,126
[WESTERN DRAWL]
YEP, JUST A-LOPIN'
THEM DOGGIES

245
00:09:20,126 --> 00:09:21,794
DOWN THE LONG,
LONESOME TRAIL.

246
00:09:21,794 --> 00:09:23,195
AIN'T THIS LIVIN'?

247
00:09:23,195 --> 00:09:24,196
[WESTERN DRAWL]
BOY HOWDY!

248
00:09:24,196 --> 00:09:26,332
[TRUCK HORN HONKING]

249
00:09:24,196 --> 00:09:26,332
[MOOING]

250
00:09:26,332 --> 00:09:27,700
[NORMAL VOICE]
THEY'RE STAMPEDING AGAIN!

251
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:33,005
QUICK, HEAD THEM
TO THE OFF RAMP.

252
00:09:33,005 --> 00:09:36,208
THEY'RE HEADING
FOR A CLIFF!

253
00:09:36,208 --> 00:09:39,078
[DIRT CRUMBLING]

254
00:09:39,078 --> 00:09:40,680
PHEW!

255
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,748
[MOOING]

256
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,748
[THUD]

257
00:09:42,748 --> 00:09:44,183
UH-OH.

258
00:09:44,183 --> 00:09:49,455
FERB, STRUM SOMETHING.
IT'LL CALM THEM DOWN.

259
00:09:49,455 --> 00:09:53,759
[MOOING]

260
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:54,961
[HORSES WHINNYING]

261
00:09:54,961 --> 00:10:10,977
Phineas and Isabella:
YEE-HAW!

262
00:10:10,977 --> 00:10:13,646
YO, COWS.

263
00:10:13,646 --> 00:10:17,016
UH, HYAH.

264
00:10:17,016 --> 00:10:19,518
[MOOING]

265
00:10:19,518 --> 00:10:23,422
HEY, WE'RE FORDING A STREAM.

266
00:10:23,422 --> 00:10:26,158
AAH!

267
00:10:26,158 --> 00:10:27,193
CACTUS! OH!

268
00:10:27,193 --> 00:10:29,095
SNAKES! UNH!
SCORPIONS! OH!

269
00:10:29,095 --> 00:10:30,763
AAH!
[SPLASH]

270
00:10:30,763 --> 00:10:34,700
HA HA, YOU MAY THINK
THAT I AM DEFEATED,
PERRY THE PLATYPUS,

271
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:39,672
BUT I STILL HAVE
MY TERMITE-CONTROLLING
HELMET. HA HA HA.

272
00:10:39,672 --> 00:10:42,575
AAH!

273
00:10:42,575 --> 00:10:44,910
Doofenshmirtz: SAVE US,
PERRY THE PLATYPUS!

274
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:47,146
OOH...

275
00:10:47,146 --> 00:10:49,815
OH, HA HA HA HA!
I SURVIVED.

276
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:51,150
WAIT, WHAT WAS THAT?

277
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:53,285
DID--DID YOU JUST HIT
THE REVERSE SWITCH?

278
00:10:53,285 --> 00:10:54,854
OH, WHY DO I EVEN
PUT THAT ON THERE?

279
00:10:54,854 --> 00:10:56,355
I CAN'T EVEN REACH IT.

280
00:10:56,355 --> 00:10:58,224
WHAT IS WRONG
WITH ME ANYWAY?

281
00:10:58,224 --> 00:10:59,592
[WHIRRING]
AAH!

282
00:10:59,592 --> 00:11:01,327
WAIT! GO AWAY! AAH!

283
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:03,095
STOP! PERRY, HELP ME!

284
00:11:03,095 --> 00:11:06,832
[SCREAMING]

285
00:11:06,832 --> 00:11:09,068
PERRY! AAH! HELP ME!

286
00:11:09,068 --> 00:11:10,569
HELP ME!

287
00:11:10,569 --> 00:11:12,004
WELL, THIS HAS BEEN FUN,

288
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:14,607
BUT WE OUGHT TO BE GETTING
THE HERD BACK INTO A CORRAL.

289
00:11:14,607 --> 00:11:16,342
WHERE CAN WE FIND A CORRAL?

290
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:23,783
[MOOING]

291
00:11:23,783 --> 00:11:25,017
WELL, THAT WAS EASY.

292
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:26,452
AAH!

293
00:11:26,452 --> 00:11:29,188
CURSE YOU,
PERRY THE PLATYPUS!

294
00:11:29,188 --> 00:11:32,358
HUH. THAT WAS SO AWESOME.

295
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:35,194
WOO-HOO.
HEY, KIDS.
DID YOU GUYS HAVE FUN?

296
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:37,596
YEE-HAW!
YO, DOGGIE.

297
00:11:37,596 --> 00:11:40,599
OH, GOOD.

298
00:11:37,596 --> 00:11:40,599
[CANDACE GRUMBLING]

299
00:11:40,599 --> 00:11:42,835
CANDACE...
ARE YOU OK, SWEETIE?

300
00:11:42,835 --> 00:11:45,371
I SO DON'T WANT
TO TALK ABOUT IT.

301
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:48,240
ALL RIGHT.
GET IN THE CAR,
SNAPPY PANTS.

302
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,308
WHAT WAS THAT ABOUT?

303
00:11:49,308 --> 00:11:54,547
I RECKON HERDING CATTLE
AIN'T FOR CITY FOLK.

304
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:58,517
[DAD HUMMING]

305
00:11:58,517 --> 00:12:01,320
SO, WHAT ARE YOU BOYS
THINKING OF DOING TODAY?

306
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:04,190
UH...WE DON'T KNOW.

307
00:12:04,190 --> 00:12:06,058
IT'S TOO HOT TO THINK.

308
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:08,728
YEAH, MOM AND I
ARE GETTING RID OF
A FEW OLD THINGS

309
00:12:08,728 --> 00:12:12,398
AT THE ANTIQUE STORE,
BUT I THINK I'VE GOT
JUST WHAT YOU NEED.

310
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:15,067
A SNOW CONE MACHINE JUST
LIKE WHEN I WAS A KID.

311
00:12:15,067 --> 00:12:16,435
HOW DOES IT WORK?

312
00:12:16,435 --> 00:12:17,436
WELL, YOU POUR
THE ICE IN HERE.

313
00:12:17,436 --> 00:12:19,338
YOU GIVE IT A CRANK,

314
00:12:19,338 --> 00:12:22,074
ADD SOME SYRUP, AND
BOB'S YOUR UNCLE--

315
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:23,409
♪ SNOW CONES
FOR EVERYONE ♪

316
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:25,444
HONEY! WE NEED TO GO.

317
00:12:25,444 --> 00:12:27,780
THE ANTIQUE SHOW CLOSES
IN JUST 12 HOURS.

318
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:30,549
OK, KIDS.
I'LL LEAVE YOU IN CHARGE
OF THE MACHINE.

319
00:12:30,549 --> 00:12:32,351
AND BE EASY ON
YOUR SISTER.

320
00:12:32,351 --> 00:12:38,357
SHE'S BEEN A BIT
ON EDGE LATELY.

321
00:12:38,357 --> 00:12:41,227
WOW. SNOW IN JULY.

322
00:12:41,227 --> 00:12:42,561
[CHOIR HARMONIZING]

323
00:12:41,227 --> 00:12:42,561
THAT'S IT!

324
00:12:42,561 --> 00:12:44,430
I KNOW WHAT
WE'RE GOING TO DO TODAY!

325
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:46,065
WE'RE GOING TO NEED
A LOT MORE ICE.

326
00:12:46,065 --> 00:12:47,099
WHAT IS ALL THIS?

327
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:48,868
IT'S A SNOW CONE.
YOU WANT SOME?

328
00:12:48,868 --> 00:12:50,870
YOU MEAN CRUSHED ICE
COVERED WITH BLUE CARBS?

329
00:12:50,870 --> 00:12:52,404
LAME.

330
00:12:52,404 --> 00:12:54,006
MAYBE PERRY WANTS SOME.

331
00:12:54,006 --> 00:13:03,682
HEY, WHERE'S PERRY?

332
00:13:03,682 --> 00:13:05,885
GOOD MORNING, AGENT P.
I'LL GET RIGHT TO IT.

333
00:13:05,885 --> 00:13:09,321
THIS TIME WE'RE WORRIED
ABOUT DOOFENSHMIRTZ
BUYING LASER POINTERS.

334
00:13:09,321 --> 00:13:10,990
I MEAN, 2 OR 3 OF THEM
WOULD BE FINE,

335
00:13:10,990 --> 00:13:13,993
BUT HE JUST PUT IN
AN ORDER FOR 18,000 OF THEM?

336
00:13:13,993 --> 00:13:17,263
ONLY A CRAZED, EVIL,
AND DIABOLICAL MIND
WOULD DO THAT.

337
00:13:17,263 --> 00:13:20,533
I'M SURE YOU'LL KNOW
WHAT TO DO, AGENT P.

338
00:13:20,533 --> 00:13:24,970
[FANS BLOWING]

339
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:26,772
HEY, PHINEAS.
HI, ISABELLA.

340
00:13:26,772 --> 00:13:27,907
WHATCHA DOING?

341
00:13:27,907 --> 00:13:30,042
WE'RE MAKING S'WINTER.

342
00:13:27,907 --> 00:13:30,042
S'WINTER?

343
00:13:30,042 --> 00:13:33,212
IT'S A UNIQUE
AND LOGIC-DEFYING AMALGAM
OF WINTER AND SUMMER.

344
00:13:33,212 --> 00:13:34,480
WHY HAVE SNOW
 IN THE WINTER

345
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,248
WHEN IT'S TOO COLD
TO ENJOY IT?

346
00:13:36,248 --> 00:13:40,486
YOU GUYS ARE GOING
TO NEED SOME HELP.
[WHISTLES]

347
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:42,421
I THINK CHEERLEADERS
ARE OVERRATED, ANYWAY.

348
00:13:42,421 --> 00:13:44,256
I MEAN,
BEING GORGEOUS AND POPULAR?

349
00:13:44,256 --> 00:13:45,658
DOES THAT MATTER
IN THE REAL WORLD?

350
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:46,992
WHAT IS GOING ON OUT THERE?

351
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:49,061
WHOA! THIS LOOKS GREAT!

352
00:13:49,061 --> 00:13:56,001
[GRUNTING]

353
00:13:56,001 --> 00:13:58,904
[GRUNTING AND PANTING]

354
00:13:58,904 --> 00:14:01,073
PHINEAS!
WHAT'S GOING ON HERE?

355
00:14:01,073 --> 00:14:02,808
IT'S SUMMER
AND WINTER TOGETHER.

356
00:14:02,808 --> 00:14:04,143
IT'S S'WINTER.

357
00:14:04,143 --> 00:14:06,779
♪ WELL, THERE'S SNOW
ON THE GROUND ♪

358
00:14:06,779 --> 00:14:09,148
♪ THERE'S SLEIGH BELLS
ALL AROUND ♪

359
00:14:09,148 --> 00:14:11,150
♪ BUT THE SUN'S
BEATING DOWN ♪

360
00:14:11,150 --> 00:14:14,019
♪ 'CAUSE IT'S S'WINTER ♪

361
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:16,388
♪ IT'S SKI AND
SNOWBALL FIGHT TIME ♪

362
00:14:16,388 --> 00:14:18,824
♪ AND ALSO
FLY A KITE TIME ♪

363
00:14:18,824 --> 00:14:20,192
♪ COLD AND SUNNY,
YES, THAT'S RIGHT ♪

364
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:23,162
♪ I'M TALKIN'
'BOUT S'WINTER ♪

365
00:14:23,162 --> 00:14:25,965
♪ IT'S A S'WINTER
S'WONDERLAND ♪

366
00:14:25,965 --> 00:14:28,167
♪ UNUSUAL AND GRAND ♪

367
00:14:28,167 --> 00:14:30,202
♪ YOU CAN FREEZE
WHILE YOU GET TAN ♪

368
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:32,304
♪ BECAUSE IT'S S'WINTER! ♪

369
00:14:32,304 --> 00:14:35,207
♪ I'M TALKIN'
'BOUT S'WINTER ♪

370
00:14:35,207 --> 00:14:38,677
♪ IT'S SO S'WINTER ♪

371
00:14:38,677 --> 00:14:39,945
[CHILDREN LAUGHING]

372
00:14:39,945 --> 00:14:40,946
[MUSIC ENDS]

373
00:14:40,946 --> 00:14:43,382
SOME PEOPLE
CALL IT "WUMMER."

374
00:14:43,382 --> 00:14:45,184
I'M CALLING MOM, YOU KNOW.

375
00:14:45,184 --> 00:14:47,186
[PHONE BEEPING]

376
00:14:47,186 --> 00:14:48,954
JEREMY?

377
00:14:47,186 --> 00:14:48,954
HEY, CANDACE.

378
00:14:48,954 --> 00:14:49,889
YOU WANT TO GO SKIING?

379
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:51,323
OH, I'D LOVE TO,

380
00:14:51,323 --> 00:14:54,360
BUT, UH, BUT I AM
SO AFRAID OF HEIGHTS.

381
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:57,129
BUMMER. WELL,
SEE YOU LATER, THEN.

382
00:14:57,129 --> 00:14:59,198
DEE DEE, WAIT UP!

383
00:14:59,198 --> 00:15:00,799
[GASPS] DEE DEE?

384
00:15:00,799 --> 00:15:03,802
[PHONE BEEPING]

385
00:15:00,799 --> 00:15:03,802
STACY? WHO'S DEE DEE?

386
00:15:03,802 --> 00:15:06,338
A SWEDISH EXCHANGE STUDENT?

387
00:15:06,338 --> 00:15:08,440
I GOT TO GO.
HEY, WAIT FOR ME!

388
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,042
Candace:
LET ME THROUGH!
LET ME THROUGH!

389
00:15:10,042 --> 00:15:12,044
OH, OUT OF MY WAY!

390
00:15:12,044 --> 00:15:13,212
[CANDACE GRUMBLING]

391
00:15:13,212 --> 00:15:15,281
MY BROTHERS ARE JUST
DRIVING ME CRAZY.

392
00:15:15,281 --> 00:15:18,717
[SCOFFS] YOU SHOULD
TRY SPENDING AN HOUR
WITH MY DAD SOMETIME.

393
00:15:18,717 --> 00:15:19,785
AAH!

394
00:15:19,785 --> 00:15:23,055
OH, I HAD NO IDEA
THIS THING WAS SO HIGH.

395
00:15:23,055 --> 00:15:26,058
[GASPING] THERE.

396
00:15:26,058 --> 00:15:28,460
GREAT. HERE WE GO.

397
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:29,828
WAIT! WAIT, WAIT, WAIT!

398
00:15:29,828 --> 00:15:33,198
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO!

399
00:15:33,198 --> 00:15:37,102
♪ DOOFENSHMIRTZ EVIL
INCORPORATED ♪

400
00:15:37,102 --> 00:15:39,104
AS SOON AS HE WALKS
THROUGH THAT FRONT DOOR,

401
00:15:39,104 --> 00:15:40,839
NO MORE
PERRY THE PLATYPUS.

402
00:15:40,839 --> 00:15:44,143
[LOUD PIANO NOTES PLAYING]

403
00:15:44,143 --> 00:15:45,878
IT'S GENIUS, RIGHT?

404
00:15:45,878 --> 00:15:49,281
OH! OH, I TOLD NANCY TO KEEP
THE BACK DOOR LOCKED!

405
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:50,816
[CLEARS THROAT]
NOTE TO SELF--

406
00:15:50,816 --> 00:15:52,851
MY EVIL DEED FOR TOMORROW--
FIRE THE MAID.

407
00:15:52,851 --> 00:15:54,687
WHAT ARE YOU LOOKING AT?

408
00:15:54,687 --> 00:15:59,792
NOT SO FAST,
PERRY THE PLATYPUS.

409
00:15:59,792 --> 00:16:01,660
DON'T WORRY,
IT'S NOT WHAT YOU THINK.

410
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:03,228
IT'S MY SPECIAL RECIPE

411
00:16:03,228 --> 00:16:05,497
FOR QUICK-HARDENING
CHOCOLATE.

412
00:16:05,497 --> 00:16:09,401
BETWEEN YOU AND ME,
MY POPULARITY HAS PLUMMETED
TO AN ALL-TIME LOW.

413
00:16:09,401 --> 00:16:12,037
BUT EVERYBODY
LOVES CHOCOLATE!

414
00:16:12,037 --> 00:16:15,107
WHAT IF I COULD RECREATE
CHOCOLATE IN MY OWN IMAGE?

415
00:16:15,107 --> 00:16:19,178
BEHOLD,
THE MELTINATOR 6-5000.

416
00:16:19,178 --> 00:16:22,881
POWERED BY THOUSANDS
OF LASER POINTERS.

417
00:16:22,881 --> 00:16:25,217
IT HAS A MELTING CAPACITY...

418
00:16:25,217 --> 00:16:27,319
OF 7.

419
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:30,155
THAT'S ON A SCALE OF 1-5,
SO THAT'S A BIG NUMBER.

420
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:35,794
HERE, WATCH THIS.

421
00:16:35,794 --> 00:16:38,263
Doofenshmirtz:
COLLECT MY HARVEST
THROUGH THE CITY STREETS,

422
00:16:38,263 --> 00:16:42,034
WHERE IT WILL BE PROCESSED
WITH MY SECRET INGREDIENTS

423
00:16:42,034 --> 00:16:46,939
TO PRODUCE THE MOST
IRRESISTIBLE CONFECTION
IN THE TRI-STATE AREA.

424
00:16:46,939 --> 00:16:50,809
NOW DO YOU UNDERSTAND
WHAT YOU ARE UP AGAINST?

425
00:16:50,809 --> 00:16:52,511
COME ON, YOU DIDN'T
GET ANY OF THAT?

426
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:54,380
YOU DIDN'T GET ANY OF THAT?

427
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,849
[SIGHS]
OK, I WILL START AGAIN.

428
00:16:56,849 --> 00:16:58,817
FIRST OF ALL, MY POPULARITY
IS AN ALL-TIME LOW.

429
00:16:58,817 --> 00:17:01,120
YOU GOT THAT, RIGHT?
OK. THEN--

430
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:03,555
ALL RIGHT.
THAT SHOULD DO IT.

431
00:17:03,555 --> 00:17:07,126
I'LL JUST WALK
ALL THE WAY UP TO THE TOP.

432
00:17:07,126 --> 00:17:09,028
NOTHING WILL
STAND IN MY WAY.

433
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:10,195
HEY...

434
00:17:10,195 --> 00:17:11,563
WHY IS IT SO DARK OUT HERE?

435
00:17:11,563 --> 00:17:14,967
OW! OH, THAT HURTS!

436
00:17:14,967 --> 00:17:19,204
WAIT A MINUTE. I GOT IT!

437
00:17:19,204 --> 00:17:21,106
[CANDACE CHUCKLING]

438
00:17:21,106 --> 00:17:23,642
...WITH
MY MELTINATOR 6-5000.

439
00:17:23,642 --> 00:17:25,878
THERE--DID YOU
GET IT THAT TIME?

440
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:27,112
WELL...[SIGHS]

441
00:17:27,112 --> 00:17:28,380
WELL, I'M NOT
GOING OVER IT AGAIN.

442
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:32,885
TIME TO GET STARTED.

443
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:34,586
AT THIS VERY MOMENT,

444
00:17:34,586 --> 00:17:36,555
THE WORLD'S LARGEST
CHOCOLATE BAR

445
00:17:36,555 --> 00:17:39,425
IS PASSING
THROUGH TOWN ON THE WAY
TO THE SMITHSONIAN.

446
00:17:39,425 --> 00:17:41,794
BUT IT WILL NEVER ARRIVE!

447
00:17:41,794 --> 00:17:44,997
IN 5, 4, 3...

448
00:17:44,997 --> 00:17:47,232
[SIGHS]

449
00:17:47,232 --> 00:17:51,136
2 1/2, 2 1/4--
IS THAT IT?

450
00:17:51,136 --> 00:17:52,805
IS THAT--YOU'RE NOT
GOING TO DO ANYTHING?

451
00:17:52,805 --> 00:17:54,506
YOU'RE JUST GOING TO STAND
THERE LIKE A DEAD FISH?

452
00:17:54,506 --> 00:17:57,009
I'M GIVING YOU A CHANCE
TO DO SOMETHING HERE.

453
00:17:57,009 --> 00:17:58,844
OH, THIS USED
TO BE MORE FUN.

454
00:17:58,844 --> 00:18:02,047
1 1/2, 1 1/4.

455
00:18:02,047 --> 00:18:03,048
YOU KNOW,
IN SOME CULTURES,

456
00:18:03,048 --> 00:18:06,585
IT'S CONSIDERED RUDE
NOT TO PARTICI--UNH!

457
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:08,120
PERRY THE PLATYPUS?

458
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,955
BUT HOW DID YOU--[GASPS]

459
00:18:09,955 --> 00:18:12,624
YOU ATE YOUR OWN HEINIE?

460
00:18:12,624 --> 00:18:24,436
[GRUNTING]
I MUST AIM IT QUICKLY!

461
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:25,571
Dad: OH, THE KIDS
ARE GOING TO LOVE

462
00:18:25,571 --> 00:18:27,406
THIS AUSTRIAN-STYLE
CUCKOO CLOCK.

463
00:18:27,406 --> 00:18:30,142
OH, I WISH YOU'D LET ME
BUY THE LARGE ONE.

464
00:18:30,142 --> 00:18:33,011
[SCREAMS]

465
00:18:30,142 --> 00:18:33,011
[TIRES MELTING]

466
00:18:33,011 --> 00:18:36,982
MAYBE WE SHOULD PULL OVER
AND SEE WHAT'S GOING ON.

467
00:18:36,982 --> 00:18:38,884
THAT'S PECULIAR.

468
00:18:38,884 --> 00:18:44,756
GOOD THING WE ALSO BOUGHT
THOSE 4 SPARE TIRES, HUH?

469
00:18:44,756 --> 00:18:46,825
THANKS, BUFORD.

470
00:18:46,825 --> 00:18:50,295
NOW, ALL I NEED TO DO
IS FIND MY JEREMY.

471
00:18:50,295 --> 00:18:51,830
OH, NO!
HE'S TALKING TO DEE DEE!

472
00:18:51,830 --> 00:18:53,165
I GOT TO PUT A STOP TO THIS.

473
00:18:53,165 --> 00:18:54,933
OH, JEREMY!

474
00:18:54,933 --> 00:18:56,235
UH, WAIT...

475
00:18:56,235 --> 00:18:57,970
JEREMY!

476
00:18:56,235 --> 00:18:57,970
WHO'S THAT?

477
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:02,341
AAH!

478
00:19:02,341 --> 00:19:08,514
WHY DOES THIS KEEP
HAPPENING TO ME?

479
00:19:08,514 --> 00:19:10,549
[TEETH CHATTERING]

480
00:19:08,514 --> 00:19:10,549
TOO SCRAWNY.

481
00:19:10,549 --> 00:19:14,887
THROW IT BACK.

482
00:19:14,887 --> 00:19:16,488
WOW, DEE DEE!

483
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:20,959
YOU'RE A REALLY GREAT SKIER.

484
00:19:20,959 --> 00:19:23,262
[SCREAMING]

485
00:19:23,262 --> 00:19:25,130
HEY, CANDACE.
GLAD YOU COULD JOIN US.

486
00:19:25,130 --> 00:19:26,765
THIS IS GOING TO BE GREAT.

487
00:19:26,765 --> 00:19:32,271
[SCREAMING]

488
00:19:32,271 --> 00:19:37,075
HOW'D THAT MISS US?

489
00:19:37,075 --> 00:19:40,913
THAT'S JUST WEIRD.

490
00:19:40,913 --> 00:19:42,214
HOLD ON.
AAH!

491
00:19:42,214 --> 00:19:49,321
[CANDACE SCREAMING]

492
00:19:49,321 --> 00:19:53,325
THAT'S THE SPIRIT!
[YELLING]

493
00:19:53,325 --> 00:19:55,227
AAH!
'SCUSE ME, BOB.

494
00:19:55,227 --> 00:19:57,095
PARDON ME, BOB,
ONE SIDE, BOB.

495
00:19:57,095 --> 00:19:58,697
COMING THROUGH, BOB.
WHOOPSY DAISY.

496
00:19:58,697 --> 00:20:03,735
THERE WE GO.
IT'S A BOBSLED.

497
00:20:03,735 --> 00:20:05,470
UH, HAVE YOU SEEN CANDACE?

498
00:20:05,470 --> 00:20:07,606
[SCREAMING]

499
00:20:05,470 --> 00:20:07,606
OH, HEY.

500
00:20:07,606 --> 00:20:10,409
HERE SHE IS.
YOU ROCK, CANDACE.

501
00:20:10,409 --> 00:20:13,812
I DIDN'T EVEN KNOW
THAT WAS POSSIBLE.

502
00:20:13,812 --> 00:20:15,480
[SCREAMING]

503
00:20:13,812 --> 00:20:15,480
HEY, LOOK--

504
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:19,418
A CLOUD ANGEL.

505
00:20:19,418 --> 00:20:25,123
NOW THIS IS WHAT
I CALL FREESTYLING.

506
00:20:25,123 --> 00:20:26,758
[TRUMPET FANFARE]

507
00:20:26,758 --> 00:20:28,060
[CROWD CHEERING]

508
00:20:26,758 --> 00:20:28,060
NICE RUN, GUYS.

509
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,394
TOTALLY AWESOME.

510
00:20:29,394 --> 00:20:31,630
WOW, THAT WAS
REALLY COOL.

511
00:20:31,630 --> 00:20:32,531
[SNORTS] REALLY?

512
00:20:32,531 --> 00:20:33,999
YOU'RE QUITE
THE S'WINTER ATHLETE.

513
00:20:33,999 --> 00:20:35,367
BY THE WAY,
HAVE YOU MET DEE DEE?

514
00:20:35,367 --> 00:20:37,502
I DON'T BELIEVE
I'VE HAD THE PLEASURE.

515
00:20:37,502 --> 00:20:38,704
[SWEDISH ACCENT]
DEREK DUKINSON...
OH.

516
00:20:38,704 --> 00:20:41,106
BUT YOU CAN
CALL ME D.D.
NICE TO MEET YOU.

517
00:20:41,106 --> 00:20:45,143
OH! NICE TO MEET YOU,
D.D. [LAUGHS]

518
00:20:45,143 --> 00:20:46,511
[HORN HONKS]

519
00:20:46,511 --> 00:20:48,547
MOM AND DAD? BACK ALREADY?

520
00:20:48,547 --> 00:20:52,818
THIS IS GOING TO BE
THE BESTEST DAY EVER!

521
00:20:52,818 --> 00:20:54,720
YOU ALMOST FOILED MY PLAN.

522
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:55,954
LUCKILY, I HAD
AN EXTRA CAN

523
00:20:55,954 --> 00:20:58,290
OF STICKY STRING
TO SUBDUE YOU.

524
00:20:58,290 --> 00:20:59,391
WHOOPS, I FORGOT
 TO PLUG IT IN.

525
00:20:59,391 --> 00:21:00,559
I ALWAYS WAIT TILL
THE LAST MINUTE

526
00:21:00,559 --> 00:21:06,398
'CAUSE IT TAKES
A LOT OF POWER.

527
00:21:06,398 --> 00:21:07,966
All: OH...

528
00:21:07,966 --> 00:21:09,968
[ALARM BELL RINGING]

529
00:21:09,968 --> 00:21:11,903
[ALL SCREAMING]

530
00:21:11,903 --> 00:21:16,275
[FANS TURN OFF]

531
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:18,343
[ALL GROAN]

532
00:21:18,343 --> 00:21:20,946
HEY, EVERYBODY.
MY MOM'S GOT
HOT CHOCOLATE!

533
00:21:20,946 --> 00:21:22,948
[ALL CHEERING]

534
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:24,516
MOM, DAD. [GIGGLING]

535
00:21:24,516 --> 00:21:26,451
LOOK AT WHAT
PHINEAS AND FERB
DID TO THE BACKYARD!

536
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:28,186
JUST A SECOND, CANDACE.

537
00:21:28,186 --> 00:21:29,421
Candace: HURRY, HURRY.
COME ON, COME ON.

538
00:21:29,421 --> 00:21:30,756
THEY USED
A SNOW CONE MACHINE--

539
00:21:30,756 --> 00:21:37,729
Dad: OH, DO YOU MIND
OPENING THE DOOR FOR US?

540
00:21:37,729 --> 00:21:39,798
WELL, HONEY,
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

541
00:21:39,798 --> 00:21:41,667
MOM, DAD, HURRY UP!

542
00:21:41,667 --> 00:21:43,335
AND IT'S A MIX
OF WINTER AND SUMMER.

543
00:21:43,335 --> 00:21:44,636
THEY CALL IT S'WINTER.

544
00:21:44,636 --> 00:21:49,074
I THINK THAT'D BE
"WUMMER," WOULDN'T IT?

545
00:21:49,074 --> 00:21:51,810
[CUCKOO CLOCK CHIMING]

546
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:53,278
YOU KNOW WHAT, FERB?

547
00:21:53,278 --> 00:21:55,480
TODAY WAS THE BEST
S'WINTER DAY EVER.

548
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:58,917
LAST CHANCE, CANDACE.

549
00:21:58,917 --> 00:22:01,386
OH, THERE YOU ARE, PERRY.

550
00:22:01,386 --> 00:22:04,556
CAPTIONING MADE POSSIBLE BY
DISNEY--ABC CABLE NETWORKS GROUP

551
00:22:04,556 --> 00:22:07,025
♪ IT'S SKI AND
SNOWBALL FIGHT TIME ♪

552
00:22:07,025 --> 00:22:09,161
♪ AND ALSO
FLY A KITE TIME ♪

553
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:10,962
♪ COLD AND SUNNY,
YES, THAT'S RIGHT ♪

554
00:22:10,962 --> 00:22:13,832
♪ I'M TALKIN'
'BOUT S'WINTER ♪

555
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:16,635
♪ IT'S A S'WINTER
S'WONDERLAND ♪

556
00:22:16,635 --> 00:22:18,870
♪ UNUSUAL AND GRAND ♪

557
00:22:18,870 --> 00:22:20,906
♪ YOU CAN FREEZE
WHILE YOU GET TAN ♪

558
00:22:20,906 --> 00:22:23,108
♪ BECAUSE IT'S S'WINTER! ♪

559
00:22:23,108 --> 00:22:25,510
♪ I'M TALKIN'
'BOUT S'WINTER ♪

560
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:26,511
♪ IT'S SO S'WINTER ♪

